  "term": "Inapsine",
  "definition": "Inapsine is droperidol, a pharmacologic substance with anti-emetic, sedative, and anti-anxiety effects. Its actions are not fully known, but it may work by blocking dopamine receptors in the chemoreceptor trigger zone and by increasing GABA-related inhibitory activity in the central nervous system.",
